	"_doc": "Race ships (Beta 3 enemy identity, scripts/space/shipgen.gd tables()): per race (a data/species.json id) the look and the kit of the ships that race flies in its own home region (a region's `race`, `race_share`). Each style becomes a faction of the enemy tables with the id of the race: it is the faction `base`'s table (the economy: costs, weights, the AI) with this block laid over it. `crew` = the race's own crew; `parts` replaces a category of the base menu (weapons, shields, engines, reactors, systems); `armour` = {tiles, factor} replaces the layers' plating; `hull` = keys laid over the base hull grammar (data/enemy_tables.json `hull`, scrap/hullgen.gd); `weights` = laid over the base weights; `ai` = laid over the base ai. `style`: what makes it read at a glance: `label` (the adjective of the name line), `roles` (the noun by size class: \"<label> <role>\"), `palette` (tint = the hull skin's multiply tint, accent = the emblem and trim, lamp = the skin's lamps, glow = the engine flame, patch = multiply tints picked per 2x2 plate for a mismatched or patchwork hull), `emblem` (a glyph in a unit box: prims of poly / circle / line, fill true or false; a `line` is a polyline of x, y pairs). A pack may add its own races in its ship_styles.json beside species.json (same shape; a race already here is kept).",
